            ("What canal opened in 1869 in Egypt, connecting the Mediterranean Sea directly to the Red Sea to bypass Africa?", "The Suez Canal", ["The Panama Canal", "The Corinth Canal", "The Kiel Canal"], "The Suez Canal cut maritime travel time between Europe and Asia by thousands of nautical miles."),
            ("What 51-mile interoceanic canal opened in 1914 across Central America, connecting the Atlantic and Pacific Oceans?", "The Panama Canal", ["The Suez Canal", "The Erie Canal", "The Welland Canal"], "The Panama Canal utilizes gravity-fed water locks to raise and lower ocean vessels 85 feet over the continental divide."),
            ("What is the only continent on Earth that contains no native human population and no sovereign nation-states?", "Antarctica", ["Australia", "South America", "Europe"], "Antarctica is governed internationally by the Antarctic Treaty System for scientific research and peace."),
