            ("What narrow international shipping strait connects the Persian Gulf to the Gulf of Oman, carrying one-fifth of global petroleum?", "The Strait of Hormuz", ["The Strait of Malacca", "The Bab-el-Mandeb", "The Bosporus Strait"], "The Strait of Hormuz is the world\'s most critical petroleum transit chokepoint."),
            ("What narrow maritime strait separates the Indonesian island of Sumatra from the Malay Peninsula, serving as the main shipping channel between the Indian and Pacific Oceans?", "The Strait of Malacca", ["The Sunda Strait", "The Lombok Strait", "The Makassar Strait"], "Over 80,000 commercial cargo vessels traverse the Strait of Malacca each year."),
            ("What historical geographical landmark in Greenwich, London, England represents the Prime Meridian (0 degrees longitude)?", "The Royal Observatory, Greenwich", ["Big Ben clock tower", "Westminster Abbey", "Tower of London"], "Established in 1884, the Prime Meridian divides the Eastern and Western Hemispheres and anchors Greenwich Mean Time (GMT)."),
            ("What is the imaginary line located roughly along the 180th meridian where the calendar date advances by one day?", "The International Date Line", ["The Prime Meridian", "The Equator", "The Tropic of Cancer"], "Crossing the line westward advances the calendar one day; crossing eastward sets the calendar back one day."),
            ("What imaginary line of latitude circling the Earth at 0 degrees divides the Northern and Southern Hemispheres?", "The Equator", ["The Tropic of Cancer", "The Tropic of Capricorn", "The Prime Meridian"], "The Equator measures approximately 24,901 miles (40,075 km) in circumference."),
            ("What line of latitude located at approximately 23.5 degrees North marks the most northerly latitude where the Sun can appear directly overhead?", "The Tropic of Cancer", ["The Tropic of Capricorn", "The Arctic Circle", "The Equator"], "The Sun reaches its northernmost zenith at the Tropic of Cancer during the Northern Hemisphere summer solstice in June."),
            ("What line of latitude located at approximately 23.5 degrees South marks the most southerly latitude where the Sun can appear directly overhead?", "The Tropic of Capricorn", ["The Tropic of Cancer", "The Antarctic Circle", "The Prime Meridian"], "The Sun reaches its zenith at the Tropic of Capricorn during the Southern Hemisphere summer solstice in December."),
