            ("What is the lowest, densest layer of Earth\'s atmosphere where virtually all weather phenomena occur and humans live?", "The Troposphere", ["The Stratosphere", "The Mesosphere", "The Thermosphere"], "The troposphere extends from sea level to approximately 7 to 12 miles (12 to 20 km) altitude."),
            ("In which layer of Earth\'s atmosphere is the protective Ozone Layer located, which absorbs harmful solar ultraviolet (UV) radiation?", "The Stratosphere", ["The Troposphere", "The Mesosphere", "The Exosphere"], "The stratosphere contains triatomic ozone (O3) molecules that absorb energetic solar UV-B and UV-C rays."),
            ("In which atmospheric layer do most meteors burn up upon entering Earth\'s atmosphere, creating 'shooting stars'?", "The Mesosphere", ["The Thermosphere", "The Stratosphere", "The Troposphere"], "The mesosphere extends from 31 to 53 miles altitude; atmospheric friction incinerates incoming meteoroids."),
            ("What scientific geological theory explains the large-scale motion of Earth\'s lithosphere over the ductile asthenosphere?", "Plate Tectonics", ["Continental Drift theory only", "Volcanic Seeding theory", "Hydrologic Cycle theory"], "Plate tectonics explains earthquakes, mountain building, ocean trenches, and volcanic activity along plate margins."),
            ("What supercontinent assembled during the late Paleozoic era and began breaking apart approximately 200 million years ago?", "Pangaea", ["Gondwana", "Laurasia", "Rodinia"], "Pangaea was surrounded by the superocean Panthalassa before rifting into Laurasia and Gondwanaland."),
            ("What geological zone encircling the basin of the Pacific Ocean is characterized by frequent earthquakes and 75% of Earth\'s active volcanoes?", "The Pacific Ring of Fire", ["The Mid-Atlantic Ridge", "The Alpine-Himalayan Belt", "The East African Rift"], "Subduction of oceanic plates along the Pacific basin fuels intense seismic faulting and volcanic island arcs."),
            ("What is the largest living coral reef ecosystem on Earth, located off the northeastern coast of Queensland, Australia?", "The Great Barrier Reef", ["The Belize Barrier Reef", "The Red Sea Coral Reef", "The Florida Reef Tract"], "Composed of over 2,900 individual reefs and 900 islands, the reef is visible from outer space."),
            ("What is the largest animal ever known to have lived on Earth, reaching lengths of up to 100 feet and weights over 150 tons?", "The Blue Whale (Balaenoptera musculus)", ["The Sperm Whale", "The Megalodon", "The Argentinosaurus"], "The blue whale is a marine baleen whale whose tongue alone can weigh as much as an adult elephant."),
            ("What is the fastest land animal in the world, capable of sprinting at speeds up to 60 to 70 miles per hour in short bursts?", "The Cheetah (Acinonyx jubatus)", ["The Pronghorn Antelope", "The Lion", "The Quarter Horse"], "The cheetah\'s flexible spine, large nasal cavities, and non-retractable claws provide superior traction and acceleration."),
            ("What is the fastest animal in the world, reaching diving stoop speeds exceeding 240 miles per hour (386 km/h) when hunting prey?", "The Peregrine Falcon (Falco peregrinus)", ["The Golden Eagle", "The Cheetah", "The White-throated Needletail"], "The peregrine falcon achieves aerodynamic terminal velocities during high-speed vertical hunting dives."),
            ("What is the only mammal naturally capable of true, sustained flapping flight?", "The Bat (order Chiroptera)", ["The Flying Squirrel", "The Sugar Glider", "The Colugo"], "Bats have elongated finger bones connected by a thin elastic skin membrane (patagium) that forms an airfoil."),
            ("What is the largest species of bear and the largest terrestrial apex carnivore on Earth?", "The Polar Bear (Ursus maritimus)", ["The Kodiak Brown Bear", "The Grizzly Bear", "The Siberian Tiger"], "Adult male polar bears weigh between 900 and 1,600 lbs, adapted with hollow insulating fur and black heat-absorbing skin."),
            ("What is the tallest living terrestrial animal on Earth, with adult males reaching heights of up to 19 feet?", "The Giraffe (Giraffa camelopardalis)", ["The African Bush Elephant", "The Hippopotamus", "The Ostrich"], "Giraffes utilize their long necks to browse high acacia leaves, regulated by a massive heart generating high blood pressure."),
            ("What is the largest living bird species in the world by both height and weight, laying the largest eggs of any living animal?", "The Common Ostrich (Struthio camelus)", ["The Emu", "The Southern Cassowary", "The Wandering Albatross"], "Flightless ostriches can weigh over 300 lbs and sprint on two-toed feet at sustained speeds of 40 mph."),
            ("What seabird has the largest wingspan of any living bird, measuring up to 11.5 feet (3.5 meters) from wingtip to wingtip?", "The Wandering Albatross (Diomedea exulans)", ["The Andean Condor", "The Magnificent Frigatebird", "The White Pelican"], "The wandering albatross spends years gliding over Southern Ocean waves using dynamic soaring to travel thousands of miles."),
            ("What Australian egg-laying monotreme mammal features a duck-like bill, beaver-like tail, webbed feet, and venomous ankle spurs on males?", "The Platypus (Ornithorhynchus anatinus)", ["The Short-beaked Echidna", "The Tasmanian Devil", "The Wombat"], "The semi-aquatic platypus is one of only five living monotreme species that lay eggs instead of giving live birth."),
